                <section class="content-section" id="sgc">
                    <h2>Service Graph Connectors (Data Ingestion)</h2>
                    <p>
                        SAM is useless without data. Developers frequently configure <strong>Service Graph Connectors (SGC)</strong> to ingest installation data from third-party sources.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Unlike legacy Transform Maps, SGCs use the robust Identification and Reconciliation Engine (IRE). This ensures that a server imported from AWS and the same server imported from SCCM merge into a single CI, rather than creating duplicates which would ruin SAM counts.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section class="content-section" id="custom-metrics">
                    <h2>Scripting Custom License Metrics</h2>
                    <p>
                        While ServiceNow provides OOTB metrics (Per User, Per Core), enterprise contracts often have highly bespoke licensing terms (e.g., "Per Terabyte of Storage Managed"). 
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Developers can write Custom License Metric scripts using server-side JavaScript. This script runs during the Reconciliation engine execution to dynamically calculate the rights required based on custom logic querying the CMDB.
                    </p>
                </section>

                <section class="content-section" id="flow">
                    <h2>Automating Reclamation via Flow Designer</h2>
                    <p>
                        To close the loop on Reclamation, developers build Flow Designer actions that reach out to client management tools. 
                    </p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">JavaScript</span><button class="code-copy">Copy</button></div>
                        <div class="code-body">
<pre><code>// Example Flow Designer conceptual logic for Software Removal
if (reclamationTask.state == 'approved_for_removal') {
    var sccmAction = new sn_sccm.ClientAction();
    sccmAction.triggerUninstall(
        reclamationTask.ci.mac_address, 
        reclamationTask.software_model.package_id
    );
    reclamationTask.state = 'work_in_progress';
}</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
